<programme channel="5e20b730f2f8d5003d739db7-65e0c8c6d899afe817b9d224" start="20251017130012 +0000" stop="20251017135511 +0000">
    <title>2 Nations, 1 Obsession - Episode 1</title>
    <category>Movie</category>
    <desc>In terms of rivalries in world sport, there is arguably none as fierce as that between the Australia and Indian cricket. -   - This documentary explores the stories behind the remarkable 1986 Tied Test in Madras, the gripping final over bowled by Greg Matthews plus the remarkable feat that was Dean Jones’ double hundred. -   - Fast-forward 15 years and the 2001 series between the nations is widely regarded as one of the best series ever played. In particular, the dramatic Third Test where a plucky young off spinner named Harbhajan Singh ripped through Australia to take 15 wickets for the match, and lead India to victory. -   - 2 Nations 1 Obsession isn’t just an epic Cricket story – it’s a tale of how two countries with such different DNA - can be brought together for the love of a game. -   - Allan Border, Sunil Gavaskar, Greg Matthews, Adam Gilchrist, Ravi Shastri and Stuart Clark are just a few of the cricket legends who feature prominently in this film.</desc>
